@startuml multicore_access
!theme plain
title Multi-Core Access Model (Single-Core Fee with SchM)

participant "Core 0\n(Fee caller)" as C0
participant "SchM\n(BSW Scheduler)" as SchM
participant "Fee.c\n(API Layer)" as Fee
participant "Fee_StateMachine.c\n(State Machine)" as SM
participant "MemAcc" as MA

== Write Request with Exclusive Area Protection ==
C0 -> Fee : Fee_Write(BlockNumber, DataBufferPtr)
activate Fee

Fee -> SchM : SchM_Enter_Fee_FEE_EXCLUSIVE_AREA_0()
note right #LightYellow : Disables interrupts or acquires spinlock\n(implementation depends on SchM generator config)
activate SchM

Fee -> SM : Fee_StateMachine_AcceptJob(&job)
note right : Reads/writes volatile shared state:\n- Fee_ModuleStatus\n- Fee_CurrentJob\n- Fee_LastJobResult\n- Fee_GcSuspended\n- Fee_InternalState

Fee -> SchM : SchM_Exit_Fee_FEE_EXCLUSIVE_AREA_0()
deactivate SchM

Fee --> C0 : E_OK / E_NOT_OK
deactivate Fee

== MainFunction (called from BSW scheduler task) ==
C0 -> Fee : Fee_MainFunction()
note right #LightBlue : No exclusive area needed here:\nMainFunction is the sole writer to\nstate machine variables during processing.\nOnly AcceptJob (in API layer) is the\nconcurrent writer, which is protected.

Fee -> SM : Fee_StateMachine_Process()
SM -> MA : MemAcc_Read/Write/Erase/GetJobResult

note over C0,MA
    **Design Constraint:** Fee is designed for single-core access only.
    All Fee APIs must be called from the same OS task / core.
    The SchM exclusive areas protect against ISR preemption,
    not multi-core concurrent access.
    
    **Volatile qualifiers** on all module state variables ensure
    compiler does not optimize away reads from ISR-modified state.
end note

== MemAcc Exclusive Areas (Independent) ==
C0 -> MA : MemAcc_Read(AreaId, Address, DataPtr, Length)
MA -> SchM : SchM_Enter_MemAcc_MEMACC_EXCLUSIVE_AREA_0()
note right : Protects per-area arrays:\n- MemAcc_AreaBusy[]\n- MemAcc_AreaJobResult[]\n- MemAcc_CurrentJob[]\n- MemAcc_AreaLocked[]
MA -> SchM : SchM_Exit_MemAcc_MEMACC_EXCLUSIVE_AREA_0()

@enduml
